  "body": "> A [body](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/sections.html#the-body-element) element's [start tag](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/syntax.html#syntax-start-tag) may be omitted if the element is empty, or if the first thing inside the [body](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/sections.html#the-body-element) element is not [ASCII whitespace](https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#ascii-whitespace) or a [comment](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/syntax.html#syntax-comments), except if the first thing inside the [body](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/sections.html#the-body-element) element is a [meta](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/semantics.html#the-meta-element), [link](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/semantics.html#the-link-element), [script](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/scripting.html#the-script-element), [style](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/semantics.html#the-style-element), or [template](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/scripting.html#the-template-element) element.\r\n\r\nhttps://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/syntax.html#optional-tags\r\n\r\nFrom reading https://github.com/kangax/html-minifier/blob/gh-pages/src/htmlminifier.js#L400 , `noscript` is missing from the spec's list of elements above where `<body>` start tag can't be omitted.\r\n\r\nMaybe the spec should say \"except if the first thing inside the body element is [metadata content](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/dom.html#metadata-content-2)\"? (Not all of those are allowed in `body`, though -- `base` and `title`.)",
